{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And the waters were a wall for them.</b> חמה is written defective, because at first the sea was filled with wrath (חמה) against them, until Gavriel came and set them as a wall within the sea. And he would proclaim over the sea and say to the waters on their right: Beware of Israel, for they are destined to receive the Torah that was given from the right of the Holy One, blessed be He, as it is said: ״מימינו אש דת למו״. He went back and said to the waters on their left: Beware of Israel, for they are destined to lay tefillin on the left. He went back and said to the waters behind them: Beware of Israel, for they are destined to wrap themselves in tzitzit behind them. And the waters would hear his words and stand as walls, and the sea split into twelve paths, so that each and every tribe would have its own trail. And in the sea-walls between each one and the next there were windows, and they would converse with one another, to set their minds at ease. Thus it is written: ״והמים להם חומה״. And according to this midrash, it would appear that one who wraps himself in tzitzit must cast the tzitzit behind him. But it seems to me that this is not necessary — what we say in the midrash, that they are destined to wrap themselves in tzitzit behind them, refers to the time of wrapping, for at that moment the entire tallit and all the tzitzit are behind them."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:14.227803692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}